\name{cellucid_filter_category_cell_count}
\alias{cellucid_filter_category_cell_count}
\title{Keep N cells of a category}
\usage{
cellucid_filter_category_cell_count(viewer, field, category, count, seed = 0)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{field}{A categorical column of the cells by name (source "obs"). A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{key}}{The column name as the app shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{source}}{Categories belong to columns of the cells. Exactly \code{"obs"}. Required.}}}
\item{category}{A category label as the legend shows it. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{count}{How many of its cells stay shown; null for all of them. A whole number or \code{NULL} (at least 0). Required.}
\item{seed}{The sample's seed. A whole number (at least 0, at most 4294967295). Default \code{0}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Show only \code{count} cells of one category, a random sample drawn with \code{seed} (the same seed and count show the same cells; a larger count adds cells); null shows all its cells again.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{filter.category.cell-count} (Filters). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{filters}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_filter_category_cell_count(viewer,
      category = "T cells", count = 0, field = list(key = "cell_type",
          source = "obs"))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
